# Modules of the stock first stage that the e5-linux initramfs does NOT load,
# taken out of the generated order by boot/stage-modules.sh (one per line).
#
# native_hang_monitor: Android's hang monitor for native processes, and a
# module-load watchdog (drivers/unisoc_platform/sysdump/sprd_modules_notify.c)
# that panics when a module's init takes over 2 s -- a fixed MODULES_TIME_OUT,
# no parameter.  Under OpenWrt the last vendor audio module
# (sprd-dmaengine-pcm) completes the sound card, the card's whole probe runs in
# its init, and on a busy first boot that took more than 2 s: "Kernel panic -
# not syncing: sprd_dmaengine_pcm.ko loads too long time", the panic's sysdump
# boot used a try of slot b, and the device came up in Android (2026-09-27,
# docs/FINDINGS.md 46).  Nothing depends on the module.
native_hang_monitor.ko
